  "plain": "In 2025, a lawyer and former intelligence watchdog named Chuck McCullough is said to have told people on a phone call, \"Well, they did it. The whistleblowers didn't,\" meaning that blame for something lay with others rather than with the insiders who had come forward. A former Air Force intelligence specialist named Dylan Borland tells this to Michels and names the filmmaker Jeremy Corbell alongside McCullough. Who \"they\" were and what they did, the telling leaves vague, but if true it would clear the whistleblowers of something they had been accused of."
